# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit real values.
#
# NOTE: there are deliberately NO SPOTIFY CREDENTIALS in this file, and none are
# needed. Phase 0 established that Spotify's Feb 2026 Web API changes make the
# official API unusable for "anyone with a public link" (Client Credentials can no
# longer read playlist items, and Development Mode apps cap at 5 invited users), so
# the app reads the public embed endpoint with no login at all. If you find
# yourself adding a client ID or secret here, re-read `docs/plans/plan.md` §2 first.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Year cache (Phase 2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstash Redis REST endpoint. Backs TWO things, not one:
#   1. the year cache, shared across all users so repeat playlists resolve instantly
#   2. the 1 req/s MusicBrainz gate, which only enforces the real global limit when
#      it is backed by a shared lock -- see api/_lib/rate-limit.ts
# Required in PRODUCTION only. Without it both fall back to per-instance versions and
# everything still works; the fallback is logged once at cold start so it is never
# silent. Setting this WITHOUT the token below logs a warning and stays in-memory.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=

# Auth token for the Upstash Redis REST endpoint above.
# Required in PRODUCTION only.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MusicBrainz (Phase 2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MusicBrainz REQUIRES a descriptive User-Agent identifying the application and a
# contact address, and rate-limits to 1 request/second. Requests without this are
# liable to be blocked. This is also the reason year lookups must go through a
# serverless function: browsers cannot set the User-Agent header.
# Format: AppName/Version ( contact-email-or-url )
#
# Required for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT and PRODUCTION -- the ONLY variable in this file
# that is. If it is unset, /api/year returns 500 `not-configured` with an explicit
# message on EVERY request, including ones that would have hit the cache, rather
# than letting MusicBrainz reject the call in a way that is confusing to diagnose.
# Put a real contact address in it: it is sent to a third party on every lookup.
MUSICBRAINZ_USER_AGENT=custom-hitster/0.1.0 ( you@example.com )
